  "title": "FDA and Gyms Warn of Health Supplements Misuse and Licensing",
  "summary": "The Maharashtra Food and Drug Administration (FDA) commissioner warns against the unauthorised sale of health supplements in gyms and stores, citing strict regulations. The regulator emphasizes that individuals and businesses must verify product claims and ensure compliance with food safety standards.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "FDA Commissioner Tukaram Mundhe has warned against unlicensed health supplement sales in gyms and stores.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The FDA requires gyms and stores to obtain a proper FSSAI license to sell health supplements.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The FSSAI prohibits health claims on product labels without proper licensing.",
