    {
      "title": "Maharashtra FDA warns gyms against unauthorised sale of health supplements",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/industry/news/maharashtra-fda-warns-gyms-against-unauthorised-sale-of-health-supplements-126112400405_1.html",
      "description": "Maharashtra Food and Drugs Administration Commissioner Tukaram Mundhe has warned of strict action against unauthorised sale of health supplements in gyms and manufacturers printing health claims on the labels of nutraceutical products.\nTalking to reporters on Monday, Mundhe asserted that wholesalers, retailers and gym operators cannot shift the blame onto manufacturers and are individually responsible for verifying that the products they sell are legitimate, free from false claims and backed by a Food Safety and Standards Authority of India (FSSAI) licence.\nHe clarified that no health supplement or nutraceutical company, manufacturer or producer is permitted to claim specific health benefits or print such claims on product labels.\nIf gym owners wished to sell supplements on their premises, they would have to obtain a proper FSSAI licence, he said, warning of strict action against those selling such products without authorisation.\n\"Nutraceuticals and health supplements are being ...",
